# Generate

## Summary
The generic AI generation verb: instructions in, artifact out. Wraps the kernel's `OneShotLlmRequestCommand` with the three-part contract every generation call ends up needing — `instructions` (the only authority on content), optional `context` (JSON facts the output must not contradict), optional `shape` (when the output must be machine-readable JSON). A shaped request returns valid JSON or throws; an unshaped one returns plain text with no preamble.

## Usage
```ts
import GenerateCommand from './generate';

let { output } = await new GenerateCommand(commandContext).execute({
  instructions: 'Create a beginner learning plan for electric guitar, 4 phases, each with 3-5 concrete tasks.',
  shape: '[{"title": string, "children": [{"title": string}]}]',
} as any);
let plan = JSON.parse(output);
```
Six shipped apps hand-rolled this call before the block existed (the highest demand count on the P1 list). Quest Log's template generation is the first consumer through the block.

## Non-goals
It does not create cards from the output — parsing the artifact into instances is the caller's (or Import's) job, because only the caller knows the target types. It is not conversational: one shot, no room, no history. Model choice defaults sensibly and stays a caller override.
